    "title": "Protecting the Fourth Amendment: Establishing Guardrails for Automated Surveillance",
    "url": "https://repwalsh.com/News/38819/Press-Releases/Protecting-the-Fourth-Amendment--Establishing-Guardrails-for-Automated-Surveillance",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Protecting the Fourth Amendment: Establishing Guardrails for Automated Surveillance\nSeptember 25, 2026\nWHAT:\nHouse Republican Policy Committee Chairman Rep. David H. Rowe (R-Snyder/Union/Mifflin/Juniata); Rep. Josh Bashline (R-Clarion/Armstrong); Rep. Brenda Pugh (R-Luzerne); Rep. Jamie Walsh (R-Luzerne); and other lawmakers will host a hearing titled \" Protecting the Fourth Amendment: Establishing Guardrails for Automated Surveillance\" to examine automated license plate reader technology and its implications for public safety, privacy, and the Fourth Amendment.\nWHO:\nTestifiers will include Lawrence Gerrity, legislative chairman, Pennsylvania Fraternal Order of Police; Jim Harper, nonresident senior fellow, American Enterprise Institute; Neal Kurk, former representative, New Hampshire House of Representatives.\nWHEN:\nMonday, Sept. 28, at 11 a.m.\nWHERE:\nRoom 418, House Republican Caucus Room,\nState Capitol, Harrisburg\n.\nLIVESTREAM:\nBarring any technical difficulties, the hearing will be streamed online at\npolicycommittee.com\n.\nMedia contact:\nNancy Nilson, 202-641-1233,\nnnilson@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": null
  },
