    "raw_text": "Walsh Announces $895,160 in Grant Funding for Projects in the 117th District\nSeptember 15, 2026\nHARRISBURG –\nRep. Jamie Walsh (R-Luzerne) today announced $895,160 in funding from the Local Share Account (LSA) grant program for public safety improvements, equipment purchases and infrastructure projects across the 117th District.\n“I was pleased to work with Sens. Dave Argall, Lisa Baker and Linda Schlegel Culver to advocate for funding of these projects, which will make a huge impact in their communities,” said Walsh. “This funding will help alleviate the financial burden on our municipalities without pulling from taxpayer dollars. I’m grateful such a large portion of funding has been allocated to our region.”\nMunicipalities receiving grants include:\n•\tBlack Creek Township - $114,522\nfor the purchase of a patching machine to repair roads in the township.\n•\tBlack Creek Township, on behalf of Nuremberg-Weston Volunteer Fire Company - $75,000\nfor the purchase of updated gear and equipment.\n•\tDallas Borough, on behalf of Misericordia University - $150,000\nfor pedestrian safety improvements at the roundabout in the borough.\n•\tHarvey’s Lake Borough - $254,308\nfor a hydrilla management project at Harvey’s Lake. The funding would specifically be used to destroy hydrilla, an invasive, non-native aquatic plant that is destroying the lake, as well as continued monitoring to determine the effectiveness of the treatment.\n•\tLuzerne County Redevelopment Authority, on behalf of Greater Wyoming Valley Area YMCA - $225,000\nfor construction of a new dining lodge at Camp Kresge in Dennison Township.\n•\tRoss Township - $76,330\nfor the purchase of a new mini excavator.\nThe grants were approved and awarded by the Commonwealth Financing Authority, which was established as an independent agency that holds fiduciary responsibility over the funding of programs and investments in Pennsylvania’s economic growth. LSA grants are derived from gaming revenues.\nRepresentative Jamie Walsh\n117th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nRepWalsh.com\n/\nFacebook.com/RepJamieWalsh\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
